Tested with **trunk r32682** openwrt firmware image.

Usb, wifi, lan, all seem to work.

This device is very similar to Dovado 3GN, Same board, cpu.


**<color red>!! WARNING !!</color>** Since trunk rev 33300, all lan ports including wan port acts as a dumb switch. There is no NAT. This is not yet fixed and it is related to swich functionality which was added from rev 33300. Everything is working good up to rev. 33298. So remember to compile your own working image.\\
The bug might be fixed in r34379 as claimed in [[https://dev.openwrt.org/ticket/12125|12125]].
A working (but maybe older) firmware from [[https://forum.openwrt.org/viewtopic.php?id=37660&p=3|this thread]]. This is an [[http://www.rosil.si/blog/openwrt-edimax-6200n/|outdated howto]].


